{"step_index":1789,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:21:02Z","input_tokens":2217,"cache_read_tokens":202285,"output_tokens":648,"tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# 3tched-container: Modular Incus Identity Containers\\n\\nThis repository contains the JSON specifications, Incus profiles, and storage automation for launching **3tchedFS identity system containers**.\\n\\n## Architecture & Separation of Concerns\\n\\n1. **Modular Separation**:\\n   * The container runtime, Incus JSON profiles, and template definitions live here in `/srv/git/3tched-container`.\\n   * The core D-Bus backend services and plugins reside in `/srv/git/odbus-verified`.\\n   * The user-facing dashboard lives in `/srv/git/3tched.com`.\\n\\n2. **Nested Btrfs Avoidance**:\\n   * The container rootfs runs on Incus `identity-roots` (`dir` driver pool) rather than native host Btrfs subvolumes, avoiding the `op-storage-kernel-guard` nested Btrfs ioctl deny rules.\\n   * Writable rootfs capacity is provided by attaching a discrete per-container image (`make-cozo-device.sh`) and running `btrfs device add` **inside the container**.\\n\\n3. **Dedicated Ext4 Partition for Cozo / RocksDB**:\\n   * To prevent Write-Ahead Log (WAL) and SST compaction fragmentation on Copy-on-Write Btrfs, Cozo's persistent store is backed by a dedicated **ext4** partition (`p2` of the attached image).\\n   * RocksDB writes in pure allocate-on-write mode (`allow_fallocate = false`), keeping sparse images compact without un-sparsifying disk allocations.\\n\\n## Directory Structure\\n\\n```\\n/srv/git/3tched-container/\\n├── instances/\\n│   └── chatbot-template.json       # Pure JSON instance specification (config, devices, profiles)\\n├── profiles/\\n│   └── 3tched-lungs.json           # JSON profile defining the /run/opdbus/lungs socket & fuse\\n├── storage/\\n│   └── make-cozo-device.sh         # Creates pre-formatted 20G image (10G Btrfs leaf + 10G ext4 Cozo)\\n├── scripts/\\n│   └── launch-identity.sh          # JSON-driven launcher: injects UUID/keys and boots\\n└── README.md\\n```\\n\\n## Quick Start\\n\\n### 1. Pre-format a Cozo Storage Device\\n```bash\\nsudo ./storage/make-cozo-device.sh /var/lib/op-d\n<truncated 163 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"/srv/git/3tched-container/README.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
