{"step_index":1795,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T13:21:19Z","input_tokens":2252,"cache_read_tokens":203534,"output_tokens":582,"content":"We have created and initialized the new dedicated Git repository at `/srv/git/3tched-container`:\n\n### Repository Structure (`/srv/git/3tched-container`)\n\n```\n/srv/git/3tched-container/\n├── instances/\n│   └── chatbot-template.json       # Pure JSON template (profiles, seccomp deny rules, idmap, devices)\n├── profiles/\n│   └── 3tched-lungs.json           # JSON profile for /run/opdbus/lungs socket & fuse\n├── storage/\n│   └── make-cozo-device.sh         # Creates 20G image: 10G Btrfs leaf + 10G ext4 Cozo store\n├── scripts/\n│   └── launch-identity.sh          # JSON launcher: creates container, attaches storage, and runs device add\n└── README.md                       # Architecture & usage documentation\n```\n\n### Key Modularity Highlights:\n1. **JSON-Native**: Instances and profiles are defined purely in JSON, ready to be fed directly into the Incus REST API or automated via a future first-class D-Bus plugin.\n2. **Avoids Nested Btrfs**: Container rootfs uses `identity-roots` (`dir` driver), avoiding the host kernel guard's nested Btrfs block.\n3. **Pre-formatted Storage Automation**: `make-cozo-device.sh` creates the 20 GiB sparse image with Partition 1 (clean Btrfs leaf for `device add`) and Partition 2 (pre-formatted ext4 with allocate-on-write optimization for Cozo/RocksDB).\n4. **Committed & Versioned**: Initialized on branch `main` (commit `6760459`).","thinking":"Modular containerization is established via the new repository, `/srv/git/3tched-container`, now fully versioned. This repository encapsulates the Incus profile and template in JSON, alongside a standalone storage builder script to configure a 20GiB sparse image. This confirms modularity and infrastructure setup.\n\n\n"}
